# Environment variable template.
#
# The Supabase variables below enable sign-in, build sharing and account
# favourites. They are optional: without them the app still runs, just without
# the account-based features. See builds-feature-docs/SUPABASE-SETUP.md and
# builds-feature-docs/FEATURE-BUILD-SHARING.md for the full environment setup.
#
# Vite loads env files by mode:
#   npm run dev   -> .env.development (DEV Supabase project)
#   npm run build -> .env.production  (PROD Supabase project)
# Both files are committed - anon keys are public by design (RLS authorizes).

# --- .env.development / .env.production (client-side, committed) ---
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://xxx.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=eyJ...

# --- .env.local (secrets, gitignored via *.local - never expose to the browser) ---
# Optional, for local maintenance scripts only.
# DEV_SUPABASE_URL=https://xxx-dev.supabase.co
# DEV_SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=eyJ...secret
# PROD_SUPABASE_URL=https://xxx-prod.supabase.co
# PROD_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=eyJ...
#
# Two email/password test users on the DEV project, for
# `npm run check:loot-filter-sharing` (refuses to run when the URL is PROD).
# DEV_TEST_USER_A_EMAIL=user-a@example.com
# DEV_TEST_USER_A_PASSWORD=...
# DEV_TEST_USER_B_EMAIL=user-b@example.com
# DEV_TEST_USER_B_PASSWORD=...
